cff-version: 1.2.0
title: pwlf_compare
message: >-
  If you use pwlf_compare, please cite it using the metadata
  from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Florian
    family-names: Rascoussier
    alias: Onyr
    affiliation: IMT Atlantique; INSA Lyon
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-3253-9814"
url: "https://github.com/0nyr/pwlf_compare"
repository-code: "https://github.com/0nyr/pwlf_compare"
abstract: >-
  pwlf_compare is an experimental C++ and Python benchmark for comparing
  implementations of non-decreasing continuous piecewise-linear function
  composition. These functions are used for duration calculation in
  time-dependent vehicle routing problems.
keywords:
  - time-dependent vehicle routing problem
  - piecewise-linear functions
  - NDCPWLF
  - function composition
  - route duration
  - vehicle routing problem
  - benchmarking
  - C++
  - Python
  - operations research
  - combinatorial optimization
  - research software
